From: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: add VLAN push support to
 hardware flow offload

ppe_offload_flow_replace() declined every flow whose egress redirect
target required a FLOW_ACTION_VLAN_PUSH -- which is unconditionally
the case whenever the router's WAN interface is a tagged VLAN
subinterface (e.g. wan.10), a completely ordinary configuration once
the physical uplink is an 802.1Q trunk rather than an access port.
Every such flow fell to the action loop's default decline branch
before nexthop construction was ever reached.

This isn't a hardware limitation: the nexthop table's C-VLAN
tag-insert fields (ctag_fmt/cvid, in struct ppe_nexthop_entry) were
already fully wired to their real PPE_IN_NEXTHOP_TBL_CTAG_FMT/CVID
register fields by ppe_nexthop.c -- they were simply never populated
by this file, and the action loop never handled
FLOW_ACTION_VLAN_PUSH in the first place. Confirmed the same
hardware-level mechanism against the vendor ppe_drv reference
(nss-ppe/drv/ppe_drv/ppe_drv_nexthop.c), which drives VLAN tag
insertion through the same nexthop-level fields via a heavier
VSI-per-vlan-combination abstraction not needed for this single-tag
case.

Add a FLOW_ACTION_VLAN_PUSH case to the action loop, declining
anything not expressible as a single 802.1Q push (a second push, or
any other VLAN TPID) to keep with this file's existing "decline what
isn't explicitly supported" style. After the action loop, if the
redirect target is a VLAN netdevice, require it to be paired with a
matching push (a VLAN redirect with no corresponding push, or a
mismatched VLAN id, makes no sense and is declined) and resolve it to
its real underlying device via vlan_dev_real_dev() before the
existing edma_port_is_edma_netdev()/dev_addr/port_priv checks -- none
of those are meaningful against the VLAN netdevice itself, only
against the real EDMA device it's stacked on. Set the nexthop's
ctag_fmt/cvid from the captured push when building it.

Compile-tested (clean module build). Not yet tested against live
hardware -- this needs a genuinely clean re-test of the LAN-side
SNAT-offload path first, given the severe, still-unresolved live
incidents from tonight's testing (see
project_flint3_ppe_hw_offload_research.md); this patch is submitted
as a code-complete, reviewed building block for that follow-up, not
as a claim that the feature works end-to-end.

Signed-off-by: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_offload.c	2026-09-19 12:01:31.317872855 +0200
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_offload.c	2026-09-19 12:01:31.318787305 +0200
@@ -21,12 +21,20 @@
  *   inbound, which is a real, known limitation of this milestone, not
  *   an oversight.
  * - Egress device must be one of this driver's own EDMA port
- *   netdevices (edma_port_is_edma_netdev()). Bridge and DSA (rtl837x)
- *   netdevices are out of scope -- on this board's LAN side, real
- *   traffic's egress device is typically a DSA/bridge netdevice, not
- *   an EDMA one, so this milestone in practice only accelerates the
- *   WAN-side direction of traffic through a plain EDMA netdevice.
- *   Extending this to DSA/bridge devices (mirroring
+ *   netdevices (edma_port_is_edma_netdev()), or a VLAN netdevice
+ *   stacked directly on one (e.g. wan.10) paired with a matching
+ *   FLOW_ACTION_VLAN_PUSH -- the VLAN case resolves down to the real
+ *   EDMA device via vlan_dev_real_dev() for the hardware programming,
+ *   and the nexthop's C-VLAN tag-insert fields carry the push. A
+ *   second/S-tag push, or any other VLAN proto than 802.1Q, is
+ *   declined -- untested, and this hardware's nexthop entry only has
+ *   a single C-VLAN + single S-VLAN insert field to begin with. Bridge
+ *   and DSA (rtl837x) netdevices themselves are still out of scope --
+ *   on this board's LAN side, real traffic's egress device is
+ *   typically a DSA/bridge netdevice, not an EDMA one (or a VLAN on
+ *   top of one), so this milestone in practice only accelerates the
+ *   WAN-side direction of traffic through a plain (or VLAN-tagged)
+ *   EDMA netdevice. Extending this to DSA/bridge devices (mirroring
  *   mtk_flow_get_dsa_port()) is follow-up work.
  * - The flow must carry a FLOW_ACTION_MANGLE for the Ethernet header:
  *   this is the *only* source this code uses for the nexthop's
@@ -218,6 +226,8 @@
 	u32 host_words[PPE_HOST_TBL_IPV4_ENTRY_WORDS];
 	u32 host_index, nexthop_index, pub_ip_index, flow_index;
 	const struct flow_action_entry *act;
+	bool vlan_push_seen = false;
+	u16 vlan_push_vid = 0;
 	u8 ip_proto;
 	int action;
 	int ret;
@@ -307,6 +317,15 @@
 		case FLOW_ACTION_CSUM:
 			/* Hardware recomputes checksums on rewrite. */
 			break;
+		case FLOW_ACTION_VLAN_PUSH:
+			if (vlan_push_seen)
+				return ppe_offload_decline("second vlan push unsupported");
+			if (act->vlan.proto != htons(ETH_P_8021Q))
+				return ppe_offload_decline("vlan push proto=0x%04x unsupported",
+							    ntohs(act->vlan.proto));
+			vlan_push_seen = true;
+			vlan_push_vid = act->vlan.vid;
+			break;
 		default:
 			return ppe_offload_decline("action id=%d unsupported", act->id);
 		}
@@ -315,6 +334,23 @@
 	if (!odev || !eth.seen)
 		return ppe_offload_decline("odev=%d eth.seen=%d", !!odev, eth.seen);
 
+	/* A redirect to a VLAN netdevice (e.g. a tagged wan.10) needs a
+	 * matching FLOW_ACTION_VLAN_PUSH for the tag this driver is expected
+	 * to insert on egress, and the actual EDMA hardware programming
+	 * below (edma_port_is_edma_netdev(), the dev_addr/MAC check, and
+	 * port_priv) has to target the VLAN device's *real* underlying
+	 * device -- odev itself is never an EDMA netdevice in this case.
+	 */
+	if (is_vlan_dev(odev)) {
+		if (!vlan_push_seen || vlan_dev_vlan_id(odev) != vlan_push_vid)
+			return ppe_offload_decline("odev=%s vlan id mismatch (push vid=%u)",
+						    netdev_name(odev), vlan_push_vid);
+		odev = vlan_dev_real_dev(odev);
+	} else if (vlan_push_seen) {
+		return ppe_offload_decline("vlan push to non-vlan odev=%s unsupported",
+					    netdev_name(odev));
+	}
+
 	if (!edma_port_is_edma_netdev(odev))
 		return ppe_offload_decline("odev=%s not an edma netdev", netdev_name(odev));
 
@@ -366,6 +402,10 @@
 	nexthop.post_l3_if = port_priv->l3_if_index;
 	nexthop.pub_addr_index = pub_ip_index;
 	memcpy(nexthop.dmac, eth.bytes, ETH_ALEN);
+	if (vlan_push_seen) {
+		nexthop.ctag_fmt = true;
+		nexthop.cvid = vlan_push_vid;
+	}
 
 	ret = ppe_nexthop_pool_get_and_ref(priv->ppe_dev, &priv->nexthop_pool, &nexthop,
 					    &nexthop_index);
